      "value": "Although the points I make here are not exactly the same as the initial feature request, they are related.\n\nCurrent camera functionality is lacking when it comes to capturing gameplay and live-action experiences. As someone who wants to become a VRChat content creator, I've found it difficult to get good camera perspectives when recording more action-oriented games and worlds.\n\nExploration, horror, and other experiences that involve a lot of movement can be particularly difficult to record. Current camera solutions seem primarily focused on capturing your avatar from an external perspective, rather than providing ways to capture gameplay while remaining physically immersed in the experience.\n\nI'd love to see the ability to **mount the in-game camera to different parts of your avatar**, such as the head, chest, or hips. This would allow the camera to follow the movement and orientation of the selected body part, providing more natural perspectives while playing.\n\nSteady-cam is currently the closest solution to what I'm looking for, but it has its own limitations. I'm a very expressive person, and a lot of my posing, dancing, and physical reactions never get captured appropriately because the recording is effectively from my own perspective. My avatar's movements are a big part of how I express myself, and I'd love to be able to capture them without sacrificing the immersive perspective that Steady-cam provides.\n\nIn particular, **a shoulder-surfing camera attached to the head** would be an amazing addition. Something positioned just above and behind the shoulder, following the head's movement, would allow my avatar's eccentric poses, gestures, and movements to be captured while still keeping the game world in view.\n\nUltimately, I'd love a camera system that gives content creators more freedom to capture both their avatar's physical expressiveness and the experiences they're participating in.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-11T02:49:03.910Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It becomes tiresome to have to keep grabbing and dragging the viewfinder around as I walk around my track space. It would be great to be able to lock it to my body or head so that I can see what my camera sees at all times, especially while streaming. I'm imagining it looking similar to the 'face mirror' except it's the viewfinder instead\n\nCurrently the viewfinder only follows locomotion, so what I'm talking about is the real life walking around my room while in VR",
